\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Motivating instance: the same assignment decision is ranked in opposite order by two evaluations. (a) The only route to the fast arm M1 is an exclusive trunk ($\mittau =6$); the slow arm M2 lies on a short corridor that does not pass through the trunk; three jobs that can be processed only on M3 cross the trunk repeatedly. The bottom gives the unimpeded round-trip times of the focal job J1 (M1: $19$; M2: $20$), used to calibrate the minimum heterogeneity required for a reversal. (b) Bar height is the instance makespan $C_{\max }$ ($4$ jobs, $2$ AGVs, same decoder as in the main text). Under the constant matrix, $C_{\max }$ is $41$ versus $54$ and the fast arm is chosen; under conflict-free routing, the same pair of assignments gives $95$ versus $60$ and the slow arm is chosen, so the difference changes from $-13$ to $+35$. All times are in dimensionless time units. This figure is an existence example; of the $1200$ parameter combinations around this instance, $205$ ($17\%$) show the reversal.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:motivating}{{1}{4}{Motivating instance: the same assignment decision is ranked in opposite order by two evaluations. (a) The only route to the fast arm M1 is an exclusive trunk ($\tau =6$); the slow arm M2 lies on a short corridor that does not pass through the trunk; three jobs that can be processed only on M3 cross the trunk repeatedly. The bottom gives the unimpeded round-trip times of the focal job J1 (M1: $19$; M2: $20$), used to calibrate the minimum heterogeneity required for a reversal. (b) Bar height is the instance makespan $C_{\max }$ ($4$ jobs, $2$ AGVs, same decoder as in the main text). Under the constant matrix, $C_{\max }$ is $41$ versus $54$ and the fast arm is chosen; under conflict-free routing, the same pair of assignments gives $95$ versus $60$ and the slow arm is chosen, so the difference changes from $-13$ to $+35$. All times are in dimensionless time units. This figure is an existence example; of the $1200$ parameter combinations around this instance, $205$ ($17\%$) show the reversal}{figure.caption.2}{}}
