\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of related work with this paper. ``Machine heterogeneity'' means that an operation has several optional machines and its processing time varies with the machine; ``corridor exclusivity'' means whether a corridor holds at most one vehicle at any time: on a single-lane corridor, two vehicles following each other in the same direction or meeting head-on may collide or deadlock, so the corridor must be occupied in turn as an exclusive resource, a modelling choice closer to real AGV shops; ``transport times used to evaluate schedules'' are the transport times the upper level uses when comparing candidate schedules: an ``unimpeded estimate'' is the shortest-path time computed while ignoring other vehicles, and ``routed (incl.\ yielding)'' is the time after conflict-free routing, including yielding wait; ``closed-loop gain and cost measured'' means whether the gain and the computational cost of putting routing into the search evaluation are measured against the open loop under equal compute.}}{9}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:related}{{1}{9}{Comparison of related work with this paper. ``Machine heterogeneity'' means that an operation has several optional machines and its processing time varies with the machine; ``corridor exclusivity'' means whether a corridor holds at most one vehicle at any time: on a single-lane corridor, two vehicles following each other in the same direction or meeting head-on may collide or deadlock, so the corridor must be occupied in turn as an exclusive resource, a modelling choice closer to real AGV shops; ``transport times used to evaluate schedules'' are the transport times the upper level uses when comparing candidate schedules: an ``unimpeded estimate'' is the shortest-path time computed while ignoring other vehicles, and ``routed (incl.\ yielding)'' is the time after conflict-free routing, including yielding wait; ``closed-loop gain and cost measured'' means whether the gain and the computational cost of putting routing into the search evaluation are measured against the open loop under equal compute}{table.caption.3}{}}
