\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The closed-loop bilevel framework. The upper level searches over assignment and sequencing with a memetic algorithm, the lower level performs conflict-free routing by time-window reservation, and an event-driven decoder in the middle translates one upper-level candidate into a sequence of transport tasks. The two feedback paths are distinguished by colour and enter the upper level at different places: path\nonbreakingspace 1 (blue, marked 1) returns the conflict-free timetable completed by the lower level as fitness, once per candidate; path\nonbreakingspace 2 (orange, marked 2) runs a trial query on the reservation table for the earliest feasible delivery time of the two legs before a vehicle is chosen, once per transport task; the trial query does not write the final timetable.}}{15}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{2}{15}{The closed-loop bilevel framework. The upper level searches over assignment and sequencing with a memetic algorithm, the lower level performs conflict-free routing by time-window reservation, and an event-driven decoder in the middle translates one upper-level candidate into a sequence of transport tasks. The two feedback paths are distinguished by colour and enter the upper level at different places: path~1 (blue, marked 1) returns the conflict-free timetable completed by the lower level as fitness, once per candidate; path~2 (orange, marked 2) runs a trial query on the reservation table for the earliest feasible delivery time of the two legs before a vehicle is chosen, once per transport task; the trial query does not write the final timetable}{figure.caption.5}{}}
