\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Makespans of the four-level ladder under an equal wall-clock budget, and the four pairs that change only one thing along the two factors. A negative value means a lower makespan, i.e.\ better. $n=100$ comparisons paired by $(\text  {instance},\text  {seed})$, two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests; $p$-values are Holm-corrected over the five contrasts of this table ($^{*}p<0.05$, $^{**}p<0.01$, $^{***}p<0.001$). The HL column is the Hodges--Lehmann pseudomedian of pairwise relative gains with its $95\%$ distribution-free confidence interval (see Section\nonbreakingspace \ref {sec:protocol}). A bold header marks our configuration; numbers are not bold because B2 is not best on every instance (per-instance results in Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:bytag}).}}{29}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
